{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox","id":1081711,"title":"Does Postcognition work on someone who commits the Grandfather Paradox?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-20T22:38:00-07:00","id":1081711,"title":"Does Postcognition work on someone who commits the Grandfather Paradox?","content":"You travel back in time and kill your grandfather before he had children, then return to the present in a world where you were never born. Does Postcognition reveal you as having a history prior to returning from your time-traveling, or do other mages see you as simply coming into existence ex nihilo at that moment, with nothing before it?<br /> <br /> In other words, is your metaphysical history tied to your pattern, or tied to the timeline of the world you're in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 04-21-2017, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T02:15:52-07:00","id":1081754,"title":"","content":"I always considered the ex nihilo option to be the case. You pretty much jump into another timeline where you never were. I also always thought that a person jumping back in time and causing such a significant event pretty much pops out of existence (from the perspective of other mages looking back in time) the moment such a momentous action is taken, although the mages on that timeline still remember him. The mage in question basically rounds a proverbial time corner on the streets of time and railroads himself into another timeline.<br /> <br /> The timelines (&quot;streets&quot;) would be like the letter Y, where you look into the past from the perspective of one of the forked branches. You can watch the mage who went into the past, but only until he causes an action that would place him on the other fork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T02:24:51-07:00","id":1081756,"title":"","content":"You can't actually commit the grandfather paradox anyway since you can't travel further back than the starting point of your own existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T02:53:55-07:00","id":1081758,"title":"","content":"Ex nihilo. I think there was a character somewhere who ended up erasing his past like that. He took something that meant &quot;Nobody&quot; as his new Shadow Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T04:17:13-07:00","id":1081774,"title":"","content":"The only way for a mage to directly commit the Grandfather paradox is to be an archmaster, since they can go to before their birth. It is possible for a regular mage to indirectly cause it by sending someone older than them back in time and having them prevent the mage's existence.<br /> <br /> But, the book says that temporal paradoxes aren't really possible. Magic takes care of the details. A mage who returns to the present where he doesn't exist returns to a world that doesn't know him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T04:57:35-07:00","id":1081781,"title":"","content":"If a Mage sent an agent back in time to kill his grandfather then he would additionally need to Shield himself against changes to the past in order to prevent being erased.<br /> <br /> I presume that the guy in the fiction sections of the core book went back via an Iris or an archmaster's machinations or he'd never have been able to erase his own past like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:10:23-07:00","id":1081784,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't need a shielding spell. The section on Time says you're naturally insulated against changes: &quot;Travelers are insulated against the alterations of history; a mage who prevents her own birth returns to a world that does not know her, but does not vanish from existence.&quot; Shielding prevents others from changing your past, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T06:27:01-07:00","id":1081805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081784#post1081784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't need a shielding spell. The section on Time says you're naturally insulated against changes: &quot;Travelers are insulated against the alterations of history; a mage who prevents her own birth returns to a world that does not know her, but does not vanish from existence.&quot; Shielding prevents others from changing your past, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you send an agent back to prevent your birth then you aren't the traveler. That's why you would need to Shield against any changes they might make. In other words you're just repeating what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:01:16-07:00","id":1081816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081805#post1081805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you send an agent back to prevent your birth then you aren't the traveler. That's why you would need to Shield against any changes they might make. In other words you're just repeating what I said.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that would make sense. I misread your original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:08:36-07:00","id":1081820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081774#post1081774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, the book says that temporal paradoxes aren't really possible. Magic takes care of the details. A mage who returns to the present where he doesn't exist returns to a world that doesn't know him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is, if you do that and return to a world that doesn't know you, does a Mage using Postcognition to view your past before the point where you returned see anything at all?<br /> <br /> I would assume no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:28:20-07:00","id":1081877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081820#post1081820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is, if you do that and return to a world that doesn't know you, does a Mage using Postcognition to view your past before the point where you returned see anything at all?<br /> <br /> I would assume no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Causality is part of the Lie. Everything Doc Brown taught you is part of the Lie. An Awakened using postcognition on another Awakened who has changed time, would see what the awakened's real history, not the one believed by sleepers. Of course this is just as I understand<br /> <br /> Also, Active Time Mage Sight can be used to detect if someone has been time travelling and it can detect distortions in the timeline. Also, I believe the only time travel spell that is Lasting is Corridors of Time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:31:57-07:00","id":1081879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081781#post1081781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Mage sent an agent back in time to kill his grandfather then he would additionally need to Shield himself against changes to the past in order to prevent being erased.<br /> <br /> I presume that the guy in the fiction sections of the core book went back via an Iris or an archmaster's machinations or he'd never have been able to erase his own past like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still go back and &quot;kill&quot; yourself as a baby/younger self, then when you return you have erased some of your own past. Your wife, child and whole life has been erased. I think this is what happened in the core story. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AmericanTypewriter-Condensed\">\u201cA long time ago, I was recruited for a mission by my master. He sent me back in time, to accomplish a critical mission.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AmericanTypewriter-Condensed\">He should have known better. I was young, and careless, and I did irreparable damage to my own history. I returned to<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AmericanTypewriter-Condensed\">a Consilium that had never heard of me, to a wife that never met me and married someone else, and to\u2026my daughter,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AmericanTypewriter-Condensed\">who was never born. \u2018Outis\u2019 means \u2018No one,\u2019 because I don\u2019t have a life outside my Shadow any more. Being Interfector<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AmericanTypewriter-Condensed\">is part punishment, part putting me to some sort of use. And when I looked at the door\u2026\u201d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>not quite sure how they managed it tbh tho, maybe &quot;master&quot; is an archmaster..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I believe the only time travel spell that is Lasting is Corridors of Time. </div> </div> </div>Corridors of time has a duration, ie how long you stay in the past, anything changed when you get back could be considered &quot;lasting&quot; but thats not really the right term even tho it says it in the book, id have said final over lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-21-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:49:05-07:00","id":1081886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081879#post1081879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corridors of time has a duration, ie how long you stay in the past, anything changed when you get back could be considered &quot;lasting&quot; but thats not really the right term even tho it says it in the book, id have said final over lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is what Lasting means. Basically &quot;everything this spell changed stays that way until something else changes it&quot; So Lasting is the correct term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T10:05:27-07:00","id":1081892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081879#post1081879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can still go back and &amp;quot;kill&amp;quot; yourself as a baby/younger self, then when you return you have erased some of your own past. Your wife, child and whole life has been erased. I think this is what happened in the core story. <br /> <br /> not quite sure how they managed it tbh tho, maybe &amp;quot;master&amp;quot; is an archmaster..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Corridors of time has a duration, ie how long you stay in the past, anything changed when you get back could be considered &amp;quot;lasting&amp;quot; but thats not really the right term even tho it says it in the book, id have said final over lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just need a Master who has mastered Time to end up in his situation. He didn't prevent his own birth, just a certain amount of his own history after that point.<br /> <br /> Lasting is the correct term for changes rendered after a bit of time travel either by the spell's Duration running out and booting you back to the present, or catching up to the present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T10:32:43-07:00","id":1081902,"title":"","content":"Outis didn't say he died, just that he did irreparable damage to his own history leaving a Consilium and a wife who had never heard of him. He may have come back to discover he was living under a bridge or sitting in prison for a crime he didn't live through committing. <br /> \u200bIn the case of Post cognition I would say that if you used his childhood home or other touch stone as a focus then no, the spell wouldn't find him. If instead you used him as the touch stone then yes, his flesh and mind do bear the marks of that history, he still has the scars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T10:46:08-07:00","id":1081908,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you wouldn't be able to discover his history incidentally, but you could find it by focusing on his personal history directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:47:41-07:00","id":1081941,"title":"","content":"This makes me realize that using Rewrite History would be a quick and easy tool to use to &quot;go on the lam&quot; for a while. Someone is hunting me, well guess what, you never met me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:19:00-07:00","id":1081954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081941#post1081941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me realize that using Rewrite History would be a quick and easy tool to use to &amp;quot;go on the lam&amp;quot; for a while. Someone is hunting me, well guess what, you never met me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it Indefinite with that being the only point of divergence from your actual life and then relinquish it. You never went on the lam in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:31:46-07:00","id":1081962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081954#post1081954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it Indefinite with that being the only point of divergence from your actual life and then relinquish it. You never went on the lam in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all I don't think time travel spells work that way. Giving it Indefinite Duration would only allow you to stay in the past Indefinitely. Once you caught up with the present, the changes you wrought become Lasting as normal.<br /> <br /> Second of all, even if it did work this way, as soon as the past went back to normal, you would, as you say, never have gone on the lamb in the first place. Which is pretty counter-productive to going on the lamb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:43:17-07:00","id":1081973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081962#post1081962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all I don't think time travel spells work that way. Giving it Indefinite Duration would only allow you to stay in the past Indefinitely. Once you caught up with the present, the changes you wrought become Lasting as normal.<br /> <br /> Second of all, even if it did work this way, as soon as the past went back to normal, you would, as you say, never have gone on the lamb in the first place. Which is pretty counter-productive to going on the lamb.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rewrite History doesn't involve time travel. The mage uses his magic to edit the timeline of his target from the present. During the duration of spell, while the new historical status quo is in affect, present time keeps moving forward. When the spell ends you do not snap back to the point you cast the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T13:46:23-07:00","id":1081995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081962#post1081962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all I don't think time travel spells work that way. Giving it Indefinite Duration would only allow you to stay in the past Indefinitely. Once you caught up with the present, the changes you wrought become Lasting as normal.<br /> <br /> Second of all, even if it did work this way, as soon as the past went back to normal, you would, as you say, never have gone on the lamb in the first place. Which is pretty counter-productive to going on the lamb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe I was talking about time travel in this particular instance so I'm not sure how your comment is relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T15:34:19-07:00","id":1082030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081973#post1081973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rewrite History doesn't involve time travel. The mage uses his magic to edit the timeline of his target from the present. During the duration of spell, while the new historical status quo is in affect, present time keeps moving forward. When the spell ends you do not snap back to the point you cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1081995#post1081995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe I was talking about time travel in this particular instance so I'm not sure how your comment is relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right you both are. I got Corridors of Time and Rewrite History mixed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T16:51:52-07:00","id":1082055,"title":"","content":"Ok, so since going back in time before you were born is impossible, you could instead satisfy the spirit of the grandfather paradox by doing things that lead to your death in the past. For example, jumping off a building in the past, then returning to the present before you hit the pavement.<br /> <br /> In that case, your history when viewed through postcognition would consist of your birth, death, and subsequent inexplicable reappearance from nothing right?<br /> <br /> That leads to a new question: What happens to your corpse? Time travel in Mage seems to involve you inhabiting your body at other time periods. Does this mean that the moment you reappear in the present, your corpse vanishes from its grave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 04-21-2017, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:15:14-07:00","id":1082062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082055#post1082055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so since going back in time before you were born is impossible, you could instead satisfy the spirit of the grandfather paradox by doing things that lead to your death in the past. For example, jumping off a building in the past, then returning to the present before you hit the pavement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that would work. History would record you jumping off a building, but since you never hit the ground it wouldn't have a record of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T18:46:52-07:00","id":1082090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082062#post1082062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that would work. History would record you jumping off a building, but since you never hit the ground it wouldn't have a record of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understand it is that when you go back in time, you inhabit your old body, and when you return to the present, your old self continues where you left off - in this case, falling to his death.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that any changes you make to the past do not invoke the butterfly effect? You go back in time, do things differently, and the moment you leave, the original history from before you time traveled abruptly returns again in spite of your changes. So the moment you go back to the present, all the people who are now in different places, doing different things, suddenly snap back to where they were in the original timeline? People who you killed while going back in time just suddenly become alive again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T18:56:55-07:00","id":1082093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082055#post1082055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so since going back in time before you were born is impossible, you could instead satisfy the spirit of the grandfather paradox by doing things that lead to your death in the past. For example, jumping off a building in the past, then returning to the present before you hit the pavement.<br /> <br /> In that case, your history when viewed through postcognition would consist of your birth, death, and subsequent inexplicable reappearance from nothing right?<br /> <br /> That leads to a new question: What happens to your corpse? Time travel in Mage seems to involve you inhabiting your body at other time periods. Does this mean that the moment you reappear in the present, your corpse vanishes from its grave?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, so the reason i had &quot;&quot; round kill in my previous post was i was trying to think of how one would kill themselves in the past as you do inhabit your previous body. Jumping off a building and returning before you hit the ground is a really good example as like you say your previous self doesnt just vanish while falling to his death. I suppose one could also take lethal poison or overdose and return before they kill you.<br /> <br /> I would say that your corpse (Pizza shaped from fallng <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) stays where it was and upon returning there is now a corpse of you and the now paradoxical you. Seems like a hardcore way for any mage who wants to be edgy and have the world forget he exists tho you could just jump off a scene ago so not much changes (probably easier wayes to fake your death or make your own corpse though), it might be a last resort for mages who are being hunted by X to resolve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-21-2017, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:25:44-07:00","id":1082112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082090#post1082090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I understand it is that when you go back in time, you inhabit your old body, and when you return to the present, your old self continues where you left off - in this case, falling to his death.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that any changes you make to the past do not invoke the butterfly effect? You go back in time, do things differently, and the moment you leave, the original history from before you time traveled abruptly returns again in spite of your changes. So the moment you go back to the present, all the people who are now in different places, doing different things, suddenly snap back to where they were in the original timeline? People who you killed while going back in time just suddenly become alive again?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is Lasting the people you killed would remain dead and their direct effects on the Time travelers life might change. But the butterfly effect isn't a thing here, the Fallen World wants to maintain the status quo. There is no causality. So the people you killed would be dead but most everything else would probably be the same. The Lie would justify this to the sleepers, but Awaken would see the effects, especially with Active Time Sight. This is a boon to a GM, he doesn't have to be logical about the effects of time travel. I don't think it is explicitly stated this way in any of the books, but it is implied at the least and frankly its the best way to run time travel and stay sane. Because of Temporal sympathy it is pretty difficult to go back very far anyway.<br /> <br /> If you used postcognition directly on a Time traveler you would probably see his original life up to the point he time traveled then you would see him time travelling and then returning to the changed future. If he actually lived it, then you would see it with postcognition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:37:27-07:00","id":1082118,"title":"","content":"I guess what I am trying to say is there is no need to try and figure out all the subtleties of the effects of time travel, only worry about the big changes that directly affect your characters.. Magic and the Lie will explain away any anachronisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:18:40-07:00","id":1082131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082090#post1082090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I understand it is that when you go back in time, you inhabit your old body, and when you return to the present, your old self continues where you left off - in this case, falling to his death.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that any changes you make to the past do not invoke the butterfly effect? You go back in time, do things differently, and the moment you leave, the original history from before you time traveled abruptly returns again in spite of your changes. So the moment you go back to the present, all the people who are now in different places, doing different things, suddenly snap back to where they were in the original timeline? People who you killed while going back in time just suddenly become alive again?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you died from jumping in the past I'm pretty sure your dead body would turn up in the present. Basically, the way to make history forget you is not to kill yourself, but to alter your history so significantly that the you that went back couldn't &quot;exist.&quot; In Outus case he didn't die, he just changed enough so that he never met his wife or made any friends in the Consilium, etc. I suppose in that case he didn't really get forgotten by history, but he felt that way because he didn't come back to what he hoped for or expected. Butterfly effect indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:35:19-07:00","id":1082136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082131#post1082131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you died from jumping in the past I'm pretty sure your dead body would turn up in the present. Basically, the way to make history forget you is not to kill yourself, but to alter your history so significantly that the you that went back couldn't &quot;exist.&quot; In Outus case he didn't die, he just changed enough so that he never met his wife or made any friends in the Consilium, etc. I suppose in that case he didn't really get forgotten by history, but he felt that way because he didn't come back to what he hoped for or expected. Butterfly effect indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div> So you're saying there would be two versions of you? One dead corpse, and one who returned from the past?<br /> <br /> I was under the impression that when time traveling, you inhabit your own body, so that there are never multiple copies of you in existence at once. But that would imply that when you return from the past, your corpse vanishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:39:21-07:00","id":1082140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082112#post1082112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it is Lasting the people you killed would remain dead and their direct effects on the Time travelers life might change. But the butterfly effect isn't a thing here, the Fallen World wants to maintain the status quo. There is no causality. So the people you killed would be dead but most everything else would probably be the same. The Lie would justify this to the sleepers, but Awaken would see the effects, especially with Active Time Sight. This is a boon to a GM, he doesn't have to be logical about the effects of time travel. I don't think it is explicitly stated this way in any of the books, but it is implied at the least and frankly its the best way to run time travel and stay sane. Because of Temporal sympathy it is pretty difficult to go back very far anyway.<br /> <br /> If you used postcognition directly on a Time traveler you would probably see his original life up to the point he time traveled then you would see him time travelling and then returning to the changed future. If he actually lived it, then you would see it with postcognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're going with this, in terms of GM simplicity, but I think it creates more problems than it solves. A clever player can go back in time and commit murder, save their friend's life at great cost, or all sorts of other things, and never worry about the consequences because only life and death changes the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:54:35-07:00","id":1082145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082140#post1082140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see where you're going with this, in terms of GM simplicity, but I think it creates more problems than it solves. A clever player can go back in time and commit murder, save their friend's life at great cost, or all sorts of other things, and never worry about the consequences because only life and death changes the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is not really what I meant. Of course there can be consequences if it serves what you want as part of your story. What I meant is no one should be knocking themselves out trying to reorder the universe every time an mage goes time traveling. If anachronisms and paradoxes pop up well that is just the way magic is. You dont have to rationalize them. Sleepers won't notice them because of the Lie. In other words don't let the side effects of time travel dictate your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T11:48:37-07:00","id":1082331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082136#post1082136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So you're saying there would be two versions of you? One dead corpse, and one who returned from the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying there would be one version of you, which would be a corpse from the past to the present. Though having died in the past they'd probably do you the kindness of having given you a funeral back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T12:03:47-07:00","id":1082339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082331#post1082331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm saying there would be one version of you, which would be a corpse from the past to the present. Though having died in the past they'd probably do you the kindness of having given you a funeral back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the book is kind of vague on this. It does say the time traveler is immune to the changes in the timeline. It does say that you can prevent your own birth and you will still exist in the present. So it isn't hard to jump to the conclusion that you might still exist in the present if you set up your own death in the past. I would probably use your logic here, unless it was a specific story I was aiming for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T12:38:24-07:00","id":1082354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082339#post1082339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the book is kind of vague on this. It does say the time traveler is immune to the changes in the timeline. It does say that you can prevent your own birth and you will still exist in the present. So it isn't hard to jump to the conclusion that you might still exist in the present if you set up your own death in the past. I would probably use your logic here, unless it was a specific story I was aiming for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also says that if you go back in the past and you die, your corpse jumps to the present (Because the spell is over) and you're still dead in the present. So perhaps instead of being buried for a long time you'd just pop back to where you were but now you're dead with evidence of having fallen off a building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:05:44-07:00","id":1083039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1082354#post1082354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also says that if you go back in the past and you die, your corpse jumps to the present (Because the spell is over) and you're still dead in the present. So perhaps instead of being buried for a long time you'd just pop back to where you were but now you're dead with evidence of having fallen off a building.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you missed that the idea was that you don't die in the past in this scheme, you set yourself up to die right after the spell ends. You jump off the building, then in midair the Duration runs out and you jump back to the present, all your changes are Lasting; including your body plummeting to it's death.<br /> <br /> You would return to a present where you died in the past (but after the time you traveled to).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:28:30-07:00","id":1083049,"title":"","content":"If you die in the past you're dead in the present. The only immunity granted to you for changing the timeline is that you remember the original events. <br /> <br /> By your logic temporal stutter cancels terminal velocity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-24-2017, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:17:25-07:00","id":1083072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083049#post1083049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you die in the past you're dead in the present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time travel insulates you from the immediate effects of grandfather-paradox shenanigans \u2014 per the book's example, if you somehow go back in time and prevent your own birth, you still exist in the present, but nobody will know who you are. It's not much of a stretch to extend that to events that cause your past self to be killed after the spell's Duration ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:06:13-07:00","id":1083094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083049#post1083049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By your logic temporal stutter cancels terminal velocity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a false comparison. In Temporal Stutter the targets present body is moving through time, In Corridors of Time you are quantum leaping into a past version of your body, leaving your current body in the present. The other obvious differences in the spell is that in Temporal Stutter, present time keeps moving forward during the duration of the spell, in Corridors of Time, present time stops moving forward until the spell ends.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:27:55-07:00","id":1083205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083072#post1083072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time travel insulates you from the immediate effects of grandfather-paradox shenanigans \u2014 per the book's example, if you somehow go back in time and prevent your own birth, you still exist in the present, but nobody will know who you are. It's not much of a stretch to extend that to events that cause your past self to be killed after the spell's Duration ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>And so the question is: Does this somehow create a second copy of your body? One &quot;you&quot; who fell to his death, and another &quot;you&quot; who returned through time? Or does your corpse vanish when you return through time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:37:31-07:00","id":1083206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083205#post1083205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so the question is: Does this somehow create a second copy of your body? One &quot;you&quot; who fell to his death, and another &quot;you&quot; who returned through time? Or does your corpse vanish when you return through time?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Respawn in your corpse's place or a suitably symbolic location&quot; is how I'd run it; nobody said faking your death through time-travel had to be easy to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T17:28:53-07:00","id":1083236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083205#post1083205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And so the question is: Does this somehow create a second copy of your body? One &quot;you&quot; who fell to his death, and another &quot;you&quot; who returned through time? Or does your corpse vanish when you return through time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it would create a second body, because your immune to the changes to the timeline. Your present self now becomes an anachronism that shouldn't exist and no one you met after your past self dies remembers you and no one you met before then believes you are who you say you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T17:35:30-07:00","id":1083239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083206#post1083206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Respawn in your corpse's place or a suitably symbolic location&quot; is how I'd run it; nobody said faking your death through time-travel had to be easy to manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't respawn, because your present self never left where he was when the spell was cast. To anyone in the present who witnesses this spell it would appear to be instantaneous and only people who had Constant Presence cast on them would probably even remember why the spell was being cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T17:50:19-07:00","id":1083241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083239#post1083239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't respawn, because your present self never left where he was when the spell was cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time travel does not imply what is effectively teleportation. Part of the niche/issue of time travel magic is having to account for any changes that occurred between when the end of the spell and the present; you can't go back in time an hour, run to the far side of town, and commit a murder with a perfect alibi. Your present self ends up where your past self would have wound up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T18:16:16-07:00","id":1083252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083241#post1083241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time travel does not imply what is effectively teleportation. Part of the niche/issue of time travel magic is having to account for any changes that occurred between when the end of the spell and the present; you can't go back in time an hour, run to the far side of town, and commit a murder with a perfect alibi. Your present self ends up where your past self would have wound up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. With Corridors of Time your present body stays where it is as you inhabit the body of your past self, your physical body does not travel with you into the past.<br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, your present self never leaves the location of where the spell is cast.<br /> <br /> Edit2: You are right if a spell ends because you caught up with the present. If the spell runs out while you are still in the past then your present self would still be where you cast the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 04-24-2017, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T20:02:05-07:00","id":1083285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083252#post1083252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. With Corridors of Time your present body stays where it is as you inhabit the body of your past self, your physical body does not travel with you into the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't care whether we're talking about Corridors of Time or Shifting Sands, because the only things the book expressly has to say on the matter are that the present doesn't move forward from your perspective while you're in the past (i.e. that you can catch up to the present rather than having to wait out the spell's Duration) and that you're insulated from the potential complications of deliberately or accidentally undoing major parts of your life up to and including your birth (i.e. temporal paradoxes are no issue).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: To clarify, your present self never leaves the location of where the spell is cast. </div> </div> </div>Again, this turns the regular casting of time-travel spells into limited teleportation despite the Space requirement for projecting things backwards or forwards to somewhere other than their corresponding location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit2: You are right if a spell ends because you caught up with the present. If the spell runs out while you are still in the past then your present self would still be where you cast the spell. </div> </div> </div>If I travel back in time three turns for a duration of two turns and run away from my present position at a maximum speed of ten yards per turn, I do not blink back to my starting position on the last turn at twice the speed I could move unassisted.<br /> <br /> If I travel two scenes/hours back in time with a spell that lasts for one scene/hour before I spend one scene/hour trekking down into a secret temple at the bottom of the Grand Canyon, I do not shortcut back to the top of the Canyon just because my spell ran out, nor does that allow me to circumvent the cursed road that makes going up take twice as long as going down without using other magic.<br /> <br /> If I travel back a year and a day with a spell that lasts a year and walk from one end of the continental United States to the other, I do not loop back to Maine three days from Vegas just because I didn't technically set foot in the present in that span of time, nor can I use regular spell control to dynamically downshift the Duration to get me back to the comfort of the starting point if/when I get ambushed by something that nearly kills me.<br /> <br /> The narrative space set up by time travel magic in other media encourages subtle or easily-recontextualized activity in the course of altering history, and treating the temporal return course as a spatial snapback turns time travel into an unassailable method of accomplishing a wide variety of tasks &quot;from&quot; the relative safety of your Sanctum. That's silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T22:22:38-07:00","id":1083341,"title":"","content":"It's not teleportation because with Corridors of Time, your inhabiting your own past body so you can only go to where you have already been. If you use the spell to go back an hour, a day, a year, or ten years, you go back to where your body was on those days. You are occupying your past self, quantum leap style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T22:49:59-07:00","id":1083349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083341#post1083341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not teleportation because with Corridors of Time, your inhabiting your own past body so you can only go to where you have already been. If you use the spell to go back an hour, a day, a year, or ten years, you go back to where your body was on those days. You are occupying your past self, quantum leap style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about your past self.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the fact that assuming a physical snapback to your starting present location upon end-of-Duration can result in physically impossible jumps of distance without the Space Arcanum or time-dilation thanks to the fact that you can keep a time-travel spell going until an arbitrary length of time before the present-time &quot;playhead&quot; and be far enough from that starting present location that you couldn't possibly get there in the time remaining.<br /> <br /> i.e. If I go a week into the past, drive across the country, and end the spell an hour before the week is up, a snapback causes me to jump thousands of miles in an hour without making use of any spellwork that actually causes that effect or indeed engaging with any of the intervening distance (and this arbitrarily does not happen if I maintain the spell into the present).<br /> <br /> That is teleportation. Unambiguously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T23:01:18-07:00","id":1083355,"title":"","content":"Hmm, what if im in my bedroom, jump back an hour to when i was still in my bedroom, i then leave and climb to the top of a skycraper, jumping off just before the spell ends. A) Am i still falling off a skyscraper when i return to the present? (Teleported out my room to falling from a skyscraper to anybody who was in my bedroom when i left (the present) or B) i return to my bedroom, my past self plummets to his death leaving a corpse,ive teleported from falling down a skycraper to my bedroom?<br /> <br /> Either way i've moved?<br /> <br /> If you travel across the country from a to b during the corridor duration then yes to somebody in the present you'd be seen to vanish from one place and appear in another but you travelled that distance normally, it only appears as teleportation to an outside witness??<br /> <br /> Still have no clue about leaving bodies behind tho, think its up to storyteller fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-25-2017, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T23:21:52-07:00","id":1083361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083355#post1083355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what if im in my bedroom, jump back an hour to when i was still in my bedroom, i then leave and climb to the top of a skycraper, jumping off just before the spell ends. A) Am i still falling off a skyscraper when i return to the present? (Teleported out my room to falling from a skyscraper to anybody who was in my bedroom when i left (the present) or B) i return to my bedroom, my past self plummets to his death leaving a corpse,ive teleported from falling down a skycraper to my bedroom?<br /> <br /> Either way i've moved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your A scenario doesn't scan for the simple reason that changing history means nobody who's looking at you in the present is seeing anything out of the ordinary because the circumstances that account for the first outcome are replaced by those for the second once the spell finishes playing out. Your B scenario is why my interpretation has temporal pseudo-suicide generally result in you waking up at the morgue; magic may be magic, but the world likes to reuse assets whenever it can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you travel across the country from a to b during the corridor duration then yes to somebody in the present you'd be seen to vanish from one place and appear in another but you travelled that distance normally, it only appears as teleportation to an outside witness?? </div> </div> </div>If you travel across the country from A to B during the Duration of Corridors of time, <i>you have rewritten history so that you travelled across the country from A to B during that time</i>. Depending on how you would have responded to being in B and what other circumstances were in play in the intervening time between the end of the spell's Duration and the present, it could well be that you managed to get back to wherever you were when you cast the spell, but it's similarly likely that you'll return to your present consciousness somewhere else entirely, possibly short several important resources.<br /> <br /> Drastic time travel is regularly a headache to deal with. There's a reason the folks who get the most facility with it also have a natural talent for manipulating luck and chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T23:41:18-07:00","id":1083363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083361#post1083361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your A scenario doesn't scan for the simple reason that changing history means nobody who's looking at you in the present is seeing anything out of the ordinary because the circumstances that account for the first outcome are replaced by those for the second once the spell finishes playing out. Your B scenario is why my interpretation has temporal pseudo-suicide generally result in you waking up at the morgue; magic may be magic, but the world likes to reuse assets whenever it can.<br /> <br /> If you travel across the country from A to B during the Duration of Corridors of time, <i>you have rewritten history so that you travelled across the country from A to B during that time</i>. Depending on how you would have responded to being in B and what other circumstances were in play in the intervening time between the end of the spell's Duration and the present, it could well be that you managed to get back to wherever you were when you cast the spell, but it's similarly likely that you'll return to your present consciousness somewhere else entirely, possibly short several important resources.<br /> <br /> Drastic time travel is regularly a headache to deal with. There's a reason the folks who get the most facility with it also have a natural talent for manipulating luck and chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, Its 7am and Bill and Joe are in a room, Bill travels back to 6am, and works out that he'll fall past his window at 6:55am he tells Joe to look out the window at 6:55am. Joe is looking out the window and see's Bill fall past the window, Bill see's Joe and ends the spell at 6:55 returning to 7am. What does Bill see? Where is Joe when he returns to 7am having skipped those 5 minutes 6:55am to 7:am? (Ignore the fact that joe is probably falling really slowly in this example).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T02:20:32-07:00","id":1083387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083363#post1083363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> hmm, Its 7am and Bill and Joe are in a room, Bill travels back to 6am, and works out that he'll fall past his window at 6:55am he tells Joe to look out the window at 6:55am. Joe is looking out the window and see's Bill fall past the window, Bill see's Joe and ends the spell at 6:55 returning to 7am. What does Bill see? Where is Joe when he returns to 7am having skipped those 5 minutes 6:55am to 7:am? (Ignore the fact that joe is probably falling really slowly in this example).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Joe's dead body on the sidewalk instantly returns to the state it was while Joe was falling, allowing Joe to get up off the pavement unharmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 04-25-2017, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:14:38-07:00","id":1083431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083349#post1083349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about your past self.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the fact that assuming a physical snapback to your starting present location upon end-of-Duration can result in physically impossible jumps of distance without the Space Arcanum or time-dilation thanks to the fact that you can keep a time-travel spell going until an arbitrary length of time before the present-time &quot;playhead&quot; and be far enough from that starting present location that you couldn't possibly get there in the time remaining.<br /> <br /> i.e. If I go a week into the past, drive across the country, and end the spell an hour before the week is up, a snapback causes me to jump thousands of miles in an hour without making use of any spellwork that actually causes that effect or indeed engaging with any of the intervening distance (and this arbitrarily does not happen if I maintain the spell into the present).<br /> <br /> That is teleportation. Unambiguously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I AM talking about your past self, because that what spell does, let you inhabit your past self. With Corridors of Time you are traveling backwards along your own timeline, taking over a past version of yourself. Rewinding time. Once again, this is Quantum Leap style time travel, not Back to the Future style Time Travel. You do not stay where you are in the past when the spell ends, unless you have caught up with the present.<br /> <br /> So here is a scenario. I'm a mage in LA and I want to travel back a week in time with a Corridors of Time spell I set the duration at an hour. A week ago I was in New York.<br /> <br /> My scenario: I cast the spell and take over the body of my past self which was in New York a week ago. I have an hour to do whatever I want, in New York. After that hour is up the spell ends and I return to the present, which is in LA. There is no teleportation involved in this scenario. I end up right back where I started.<br /> <br /> Your Scenario (if I am understanding you correctly, which assumes you stay where you are when the spell ends): I cast the spell and take over the body of my past self which was in New York a week ago. I have an hour to do whatever I want, in New York. After that hour is up the spell ends and I return to the present, but since I stay where I am when the spell ends I am now in New York in the present. In your scenario I just teleported from LA to New York using a Time spell.<br /> <br /> A third scenario: You don't actually travel back along your timeline you stay put where you are in the present. I cast the spell and take over the body of my past self which was in New York a week ago, but I stay in LA. Because the spell explicitly says you inhabit your past body, that means I just teleported my past self to LA.<br /> <br /> So, which of these scenarios is the correct one when using Corridors of Time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T07:00:16-07:00","id":1083444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083431#post1083431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I AM talking about your past self, because that what spell does, let you inhabit your past self. With Corridors of Time you are traveling backwards along your own timeline, taking over a past version of yourself. Rewinding time. Once again, this is Quantum Leap style time travel, not Back to the Future style Time Travel. You do not stay where you are in the past when the spell ends, unless you have caught up with the present.<br /> <br /> So here is a scenario. I'm a mage in LA and I want to travel back a week in time with a Corridors of Time spell I set the duration at an hour. A week ago I was in New York.<br /> <br /> <i>My scenario: I cast the spell and take over the body of my past self which was in New York a week ago. I have an hour to do whatever I want, in New York. After that hour is up the spell ends and I return to the present, which is in LA. There is no teleportation involved in this scenario. I end up right back where I started.</i><br /> <br /> So, which of these scenarios is the correct one when using Corridors of Time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaning towards this one, you basically pause the present travel to the past, go do whatever you want in the past till the spell ends, return to the present,un pause and have to deal with whatever you changed while back in the past even if your not 100% sure what happened in the time between the spell ending and the present. Imagine if you were to go back a month for an hour to break up with your girlfriend only to discover when you return that you now have another girlfriend you dont remember meeting, but whom you must have met and liked in the intervening month...might be a dick move by a ST if your sole purpose was to go back and become single but fuck, time travel is messy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is that how it works, or do you get the memories of what happened along side the original memories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-25-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T07:35:41-07:00","id":1083450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083431#post1083431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I AM talking about your past self, because that what spell does, let you inhabit your past self. With Corridors of Time you are traveling backwards along your own timeline, taking over a past version of yourself. Rewinding time. Once again, this is Quantum Leap style time travel, not Back to the Future style Time Travel. You do not stay where you are in the past when the spell ends, unless you have caught up with the present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying you stay where you are in the past when the spell ends, I'm saying that if the changes you made to the past would result in you ending up somewhere else by the time the present rolls around again, you return to the present there instead.<br /> <br /> Your example is not teleportation. Your example as characterized through the outcome you expect my reading to result in is you retroactively having never left New York. Nobody in the present is seeing you disappear from LA and reappear in New York.<br /> <br /> If your changes didn't alter the circumstances that caused/allowed you to get to LA in the intervening week then you very likely wind up still in LA in the present, though the specifics may be slightly different; if your changes were more drastic (or if past-you is a shameless contrarian), you could well come back to find you wound up staying in Alberta with your cabalmate's relatives instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083444#post1083444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaning towards this one, you basically pause the present travel to the past, go do whatever you want in the past till the spell ends, return to the present,un pause and have to deal with whatever you changed while back in the past even if your not 100% sure what happened in the time between the spell ending and the present. Imagine if you were to go back a month for an hour to break up with your girlfriend only to discover when you return that you now have another girlfriend you dont remember meeting, but whom you must have met and liked in the intervening month...might be a dick move by a ST if your sole purpose was to go back and become single but fuck, time travel is messy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is that how it works, or do you get the memories of what happened along side the original memories?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the size of it, yeah. There's a reason the two biggest Acanthus archetypes are &quot;obsessive microplanner&quot; and &quot;uncaring agent of mayhem.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:14:51-07:00","id":1083460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083444#post1083444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaning towards this one, you basically pause the present travel to the past, go do whatever you want in the past till the spell ends, return to the present,un pause and have to deal with whatever you changed while back in the past even if your not 100% sure what happened in the time between the spell ending and the present. Imagine if you were to go back a month for an hour to break up with your girlfriend only to discover when you return that you now have another girlfriend you dont remember meeting, but whom you must have met and liked in the intervening month...might be a dick move by a ST if your sole purpose was to go back and become single but fuck, time travel is messy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is basically what I am saying happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083444#post1083444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that how it works, or do you get the memories of what happened along side the original memories?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good question, that isn't addressed well by the book. My thought is that you would be aware of the changes in an overall vague sense, but may not necessarily have real specific memories. Though if the player's whole purpose for going back in time was to break up with a girlfriend and stay single in the intervening time, it would definitely be a dick move by the GM to show back up in the present with a different girlfriend. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:14:51-07:00","id":1083461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083444#post1083444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaning towards this one, you basically pause the present travel to the past, go do whatever you want in the past till the spell ends, return to the present,un pause and have to deal with whatever you changed while back in the past even if your not 100% sure what happened in the time between the spell ending and the present. Imagine if you were to go back a month for an hour to break up with your girlfriend only to discover when you return that you now have another girlfriend you dont remember meeting, but whom you must have met and liked in the intervening month...might be a dick move by a ST if your sole purpose was to go back and become single but fuck, time travel is messy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is basically what I am saying happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083444#post1083444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that how it works, or do you get the memories of what happened along side the original memories?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good question, that isn't addressed well by the book. My thought is that you would be aware of the changes in an overall vague sense, but may not necessarily have real specific memories. Though if the player's whole purpose for going back in time was to break up with a girlfriend and stay single in the intervening time, it would definitely be a dick move by the GM to show back up in the present with a different girlfriend. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:32:40-07:00","id":1083470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083450#post1083450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your changes didn't alter the circumstances that caused/allowed you to get to LA in the intervening week then you very likely wind up still in LA in the present, though the specifics may be slightly different; if your changes were more drastic (or if past-you is a shameless contrarian), you could well come back to find you wound up staying in Alberta with your cabalmate's relatives instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if the point of going back in time is to keep yourself from going to LA, then yes you are right and you would return to the present in NYC. But, does the book not says that magic doesn't care about causality and it basically says the time traveler is immune to it? In the majority of cases you will return to exactly where you left to a present that almost looks exactly like the one you left, even if it doesn't necessarily make sense. The things you changed will have changed but ancillary things will remain the same, because magic doesn't care about cause and effect. There is no butterfly effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:36:21-07:00","id":1083504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1081711-does-postcognition-work-on-someone-who-commits-the-grandfather-paradox?p=1083470#post1083470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if the point of going back in time is to keep yourself from going to LA, then yes you are right and you would return to the present in NYC. But, does the book not says that magic doesn't care about causality and it basically says the time traveler is immune to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says that you're immune to the grandfather paradox and its related complications, which does not imply anything on the level of subverting spatial continuity. Being able to return to the present regardless of what you do as long as you survive the trip does not scan to being able to preserve all of your assets against warping without effort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the majority of cases you will return to exactly where you left to a present that almost looks exactly like the one you left, even if it doesn't necessarily make sense. The things you changed will have changed but ancillary things will remain the same, because magic doesn't care about cause and effect. <b>There is no butterfly effect.</b> </div> </div> </div>This is blatantly false, as Outis can attest.<br /> <br /> Stable-time-loop-style &quot;you come back in the circumstances you left and get news of successful adjustment when you go and look&quot; is an optimal result that characters seeking to make careful changes aim for, not the ground state of Awakened time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}